# What the release's own suites leave out on Android alone, in the format of
# `upstream.allow`, to which `tests/common/suites.rs` adds it there. The tests run on a phone
# in `/data/local/tmp` (`cargo xtask android-test`).

# Every test of the file makes a hard link in its setup, which SELinux refuses to the shell
# in `/data/local/tmp`.
ruby/test_file_exhaustive.rb

# bionic has no `crypt(3)`: `String#crypt` raises `NotImplementedError` (PATCHES.md, patch 49).
ruby/test_string.rb#test_crypt

# Expects the `[BUG]` report of a child that sends itself SIGSEGV. The dynamic linker of
# Android installs the crash handler of debuggerd in every process, and Ruby installs its own
# handler only where it finds the default one (`install_sighandler` of `signal.c`), so the
# child ends by the signal without the report.
ruby/test_rubyoptions.rb#test_segv_test
